### BookNook API: try every route from VS Code
### Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then click "Send Request" above any request.
###
### HOW TO GET A TOKEN
###  1. Run the client (npm run dev) and log in at http://localhost:3000/login
###  2. Open http://localhost:3000/dev/token and click Copy
###  3. Paste it below as @token (it expires after about 15 minutes: click "New token" and copy again)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### After GET /books, copy a book _id here. After POST /borrows, copy the borrow _id.
@bookId = PASTE_A_BOOK_ID
@borrowId = PASTE_A_BORROW_ID


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Health
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. GET /books  (public)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### New Arrivals: newest 6
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?sort=latest&limit=6

### Only the books added by one reader (used by My Books)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?email=maya@example.com


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. GET /books/:id  (login required)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. POST /books  (login required)
### The owner (userName / userEmail) is taken from your token.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My Test Book",
  "author": "Test Author",
  "category": "Fiction",
  "image": "https://i.ibb.co/placeholder/cover.jpg",
  "description": "A short description of at least ten characters.",
  "totalCopies": 3
}

### Invalid category -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad Book",
  "author": "Test Author",
  "category": "Cooking",
  "image": "https://i.ibb.co/placeholder/cover.jpg",
  "description": "A short description of at least ten characters.",
  "totalCopies": 3
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. PATCH /books/:id  (owner only)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My Test Book (2nd edition)",
  "totalCopies": 4
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. DELETE /books/:id  (owner only, nothing may be borrowed)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. POST /borrows  (borrow a book for 7 days)
### Run it twice to see the "already borrowed" error (409).
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/borrows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": "{{bookId}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. GET /borrows  (only YOUR borrows)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/borrows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. DELETE /borrows/:id  (return the book)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/borrows/{{borrowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
